---
description: Require architecture and planning discipline for complex changes
globs: ["src/**/*.py", "scripts/**/*.py", "docs/**/*.md"]
---

For complex features, refactors, or data-flow changes:
- use `@architect` before implementation when architecture is unclear or sensitive
- use `@validation_planner` after `@architect` for architecture-sensitive or runtime-sensitive work
- use `@planner` only after the architecture gate is approved when a validation gate is required

Architecture-sensitive means changes touching:
- collection flow
- telemetry assignment
- segmentation
- CSV contracts
- metadata propagation
- Stage A / Stage B data flow
- validation logic
- hardware lifecycle
- runtime phase/state transitions
- power/radar/oven interaction timing

